# TEMPLATE. Copy to the host's alert.env (root-only, mode 0600). The owner fills in the values on the host; this file holds NO value and NO secret, and neither does the repository.
#
# Delivery: a command that reads the message on standard input and exits 0 only when it has handed the message to the channel. Exit 0 proves the hand-off, not that anybody read it.
DFL_ALERT_DELIVER_CMD=
# Optional off-host "I am alive" ping run on every poll (a dead-man's switch: an outside service alerts on its SILENCE, which is the only thing that sees the host itself die).
DFL_ALERT_PING_CMD=
# Optional: the monitor's heartbeat file (read by stat only). Without it a stale heartbeat is not detected, but a monitor that is not running still is.
DFL_ALERT_HEARTBEAT=
# Optional tuning (defaults: heartbeat_max 120 s, reminder 3600 s, polls before "monitor not running" 2, lock wait 60 s, label = hostname).
DFL_ALERT_HEARTBEAT_MAX_S=
DFL_ALERT_REMIND_S=
DFL_ALERT_POLLS_DOWN=
DFL_ALERT_LOCK_WAIT_S=
DFL_ALERT_HOST_LABEL=
